<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">New Book of Tang</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1060</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Xin Tangshu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The New Book of Tang is an official history of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang dynasty</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, compiled by Ouyang Xiu and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> Qi and completed in 1060. Written to replace the earlier Old Book of Tang, it is one of the Twenty-Four Histories. Its accounts of foreign lands include early descriptions of kingdoms in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southeast-asia">Southeast Asia</a>, such as Holing, or Kalingga, on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/new-book-of-tang.jpg" alt="New Book of Tang" width="320" height="258" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%AE%8B%E5%88%BB%E6%9C%AC%E3%80%8A%E7%9F%B3%E5%A3%81%E7%B2%BE%E8%88%8D%E9%9F%B3%E6%B3%A8%E5%94%90%E4%B9%A6%E8%AF%A6%E8%8A%82%E3%80%8B%E5%8D%B7%E4%B8%80%E5%8F%8A%E5%8D%B7%E4%BA%8C%E7%99%BE.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
